UPM is a wrapper around Chimera Linux build system and package manager, that adds these features:
, UPM updates packages atomically and automatically
, distributed package repositories, using Gnunet
, an installer script to easily install a Chimera based Linux system, using Uni and SwayShell as user interface

SwayShell provides a graphical shell on top of Sway Wayland compositor
there is an application launcher which can be toggled by pressing "super" (mod+mod) or "alt+tab"
press the letters corresponding to an application's name (or just use the arrow keys) to select it, then press "space"
applications will be opened in their own workspace
	any extra windows opened by the application, will be shown in a modal popup
to close a window, press "super+backspace" or "alt+escape"

pressing "apostrophe" or "semicolon" in application launcher, activates super prompt
by typing special keywords in the super prompt, you have a fast access to various small but useful things like:
	mathematical calculations, unit conversions, timer, date at different timezones, weather, dictionary, encyclopedia, etc

in application launcher the item selected by default is the system menu
, session (lock, suspend, exit, reboot, poweroff)
, connections
, timezone
, passwords
, packages (install, remove, update, create an installation media)
, backup (create, restore)

to have a really fail'safe system, redundant units are necessary
you can create a backup on a removable storage device
backups will be done using "BTRFS send", so they will be incremental and fast
the backup device is encrypted, and contains a backup of your home directory
	dencryption can be done using a password, as well as a key stored on the computer
each time the device is connected, the backup procedure will be run automatically
even in case of bit rot for data in home directory, this procedure repairs it automatically
this backup can easily be restored on a new system
these systems will then form an F2F network using GNUnet, through which they will be synced to each other

first we must create a bootable installer on a removable storage device
to do that, we must be in a Linux system with these programs installed:
	curl (or wget) mkfs.vfat (dosfstools)
to bootstrap from source, these extra programs are required too:
	clang git ssh-keygen
now create the bootable installer by running this command:
; sh upm/mkinst.sh
then boot into the installer, and follow the instructions
